.SH SYNOPSIS
.IP
.EX
#include \f[B]\(dqbashclient.h\(dq\f[R]

int bc_state_set_var(bc_client_t *c, const char *name,
                     const char *value,
                     const char *const *attributes,
                     int num_attrs);
.EE
.SH DESCRIPTION
Sets or creates a shell variable on the bash\-server session associated
with the client connection \f[B]c\f[R].
If the variable already exists, its value and attributes are replaced.
If it does not exist, a new variable is created.
.PP
The function sends a \f[CR]set\f[R] request on the STATE channel
(\f[CR]CHAN_STATE\f[R], channel 2) with namespace
\f[CR]\(dqvar\(dq\f[R], the variable name, its value, and an optional
list of attribute strings.
.PP
Attributes control shell\-level properties of the variable.
The following attribute strings are recognized by bash\-server:
.PP
