.SH NOTES
.IP \(bu 2
Setting a variable replaces both its value and its attributes.
If you want to preserve existing attributes, first retrieve them with
\f[CR]bc_state_get_var()\f[R], then pass them back along with any
additions.
.IP \(bu 2
The \f[B]value\f[R] parameter is always a string.
For integer variables (attribute \f[CR]\(dqinteger\(dq\f[R]), the server
performs arithmetic evaluation on the string value at assignment time.
.IP \(bu 2
Variable names are case\-sensitive.
\f[CR]\(dqPATH\(dq\f[R] and \f[CR]\(dqpath\(dq\f[R] are distinct
variables.
.IP \(bu 2
The function uses the v2 binary protocol.
The STATE channel request includes \f[CR]\(dqop\(dq: \(dqset\(dq\f[R],
\f[CR]\(dqns\(dq: \(dqvar\(dq\f[R], \f[CR]\(dqname\(dq\f[R],
\f[CR]\(dqvalue\(dq\f[R], and optionally \f[CR]\(dqattributes\(dq\f[R]
fields.
.IP \(bu 2
A single \f[CR]bc_client_t\f[R] must not be used concurrently from
multiple threads.
